  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Patients, labs and institutions pay for safe, accurate work. They judge you by care, accuracy and accountability.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing clear, honest notes.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and biotechnology vs medicine: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools summarise papers and draft reports. Routine summaries shrink first.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, ethics and accountability hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to read and organise; later, own the decisions.
  </p>

